 "provenance": "Prediction results of the WP7 acceptance-2 fixture (test_wp7_missing_data.prediction_fixture), captured by running the fit stage at commit 514336c (turbotab-next before WP7) with OMP_NUM_THREADS=2: every family's cross-validated scores, its training-fit coefficients, and the sealed held-out scores. The elastic net's entries were captured again on 2026-10-08 in the same way, at 514336c with three changes from fix/elastic-net-determinism: its elastic_net.py and wide.py (a coordinate-descent tolerance of 1e-12, and the penalty chosen on the pooled inner loss, rounded to 1e-9), and its row_keys in inner_cv.py (numbers hashed in single precision), on macOS arm64 with Accelerate. That run reproduced the linear and boosted-trees entries to 4.4e-16. The elastic net's entries were captured again on 2026-10-10 on feat/wave-c6a2-int (C6a phase 2): RT-1b threads the split's seed (707 here) into every fit (RECIPES F15), where fits had used seed 0, so the elastic net's seeded inner folds are drawn anew. turbotab-next 05325dca with only fit_pipeline's seed set to 707 gives the same numbers; linear and boosted trees still match the stored entries to 4.7e-11. The elastic net's entries were captured again on 2026-10-10 on feat/wave-c6a3-int (C6a phase 3): RT-5f puts the elastic net on the path search with each split's own lambda_max and codes every level of a category (full coding, so gender_female joins its coefficients); linear and boosted trees still match the stored entries to 4.7e-11.",
